      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE TOP BAR (1) is knocking on the door of another win, finishing nicely from well back over 1300m last time out. A better draw last this time helps his chances with the rise in trip suiting. Can sit closer this time around and get the job done. CHANTILLY GIRL (2) was on the quick turnaround at Port Hedland last time out and was far too good, running away to win by 6.1L. Webster's claim helps and she should be able to take up the running under this scenario. Can repeat the dose without surprising. MAGIC SHOT (3) was out of the money two runs back then again missed the frame last start when he was never in contention over 1205m at Roebourne, beaten 3.5 lengths into sixth. Looks well placed so expect a big run this time. MATSOKA (4) missed the placings two runs back then improved last start but found a couple better over 1615m at this track, beaten 5 lengths. Placed to advantage so anticipating another big run. SCHUHBECK (5) is next best.",
